"The source lettered articles with Assamese letters: 21A is ২১ক and 371B is ৩৭১খ. Lessons must show both forms.",
"The contents spell some words in two ways: মন্ত্ৰীপৰিষদ and মন্ত্ৰী-পৰিষদ; অনুসূচিত and অনুসূচীত. Part XXII is headed দ্বাবিংশ ভাগ where other Parts use অংশ. An editor should choose one form for the course.",
"Terms were taken from headings, so they are the source's headings, not necessarily the everyday words a learner knows.",
"articleHeadings is a selection for the pilot lessons and common exam articles. scripts/add_article_entities.py turns it into article entities; add a heading here to add an entity.",
"Words in the pilot lessons beyond this glossary, such as ধন বিধেয়ক for Money Bill, জিলা পৰিষদ for District Council and ঝুম for jhum, were not looked up in the Assamese edition. Check them against Articles 109 to 111 and the Sixth Schedule in review."
